ref='Bonferroni controls familywise error: the chance of at least one false rejection among true nulls is at most family alpha when individual p-values are valid. Tests need not be independent for the union bound. Declare the complete family and compare each p with alpha divided by the number of tests, including equality. Main five p-values 0.009, 0.012, 0.3, 0.4, 0.8 use cutoff 0.01; only 0.009 rejects. Separate picture p-values 0.004, 0.012, 0.02, 0.08, 0.4, 0.9 use six-test cutoff 1/120, approximately 0.00833; only 0.004 rejects. Changed ten-test family has cutoff 0.005, with four outcomes missing; only 0.004 among supplied values rejects, and the other four decisions are unknown. Keep those tests in the denominator and disclose missing results. The scenarios are stipulated, not actual experiments. An adjusted p-value is min(1, m × p). Adjustment cannot validate invalid p-values, hide outcome-driven selection, prove non-rejected nulls or establish useful effect sizes. The error bound can be conservative and is not an observed error rate.'
